codex-run: --spec or --prompt is required
Usage:
  codex-run.sh --dir <path> (--spec <file> | --prompt <text>)
               [--sandbox read-only|workspace-write] [--effort low|medium|high]
               [--timeout SECONDS] [--log <path>]

Every run launches, under `timeout`, with stdin from /dev/null:
  codex exec -C <dir> --skip-git-repo-check -s <sandbox>
             -c model_reasoning_effort=<effort> --output-last-message <log>.final "<prompt>"
and writes <log>.done with the exit code when it stops, so a caller polls for the marker
instead of guessing from log stability.

Exit codes: 0 done, 75 ChatGPT usage cap, 124 killed on the timeout, otherwise codex's own.
